From 131000f7937793a31473e86d175e4f1656704105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:02:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] SaveVsmOnResult: store online battle results like offline
 ones

Online battles (Class, Mix, Fes) only stored the badge and the class
rate / class / grade, so internet games never reached the card's battle
history or statistics. With OnlineMatching.PersistOnlineBattleResults
(default true) the result now goes through the offline save commands:
battle history, win/loss (total + class / Free (Mix) / Fes), player
statistics, per-suit statistics, burst-type statistics and challenge
counters. PersistOnlineProgress (default true) also applies GP, level
exp, navigator, mastery and team points; each battle sends one save
only (online: SaveVsmOnResult, in-store: SaveVsmResult), so nothing is
applied twice. Class win/loss stays counted once by the class
persistence.

Retries of the same result (card + room_id + played_at + suit + mode)
are ignored: in-memory for 2 h, and after a restart via the stored
history row. Saves are serialised and run in one transaction; on a
failure only the old badge + class part is kept. Flag off = previous
behaviour. No schema change.

New Tests/Server.Tests (15, in-memory SQLite with all migrations):
Class solo/team, Mix, Fes, other modes, retry dedupe, flags off,
failure rollback. Matchmaking.Tests 423/423, cross-server e2e 103/103.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
