+## Online battle results (2026-11-16, branch `online-results-save`) — DB tests only, not yet tried in-game
+Before this, an online battle (`SaveVsmOnResult`) stored only the badge and, for Class Match, rate / class / grade /
+class win-lose. Internet games never reached the card's battle history or stats. Now, with
+`OnlineMatching.PersistOnlineBattleResults` (default `true`), the result goes through the same save commands as an
+offline `SaveVsmResult`:
+
+| Stored | Detail |
+|---|---|
+| Battle history (View Card → battle history) | one row per battle: mode, win/lose, stage, time, score, damage, burst, suit, partner and human foes (CPU stand-ins are not listed), action log |
+| Win / loss record | `TotalWin/Lose` for every online battle, plus Class solo / team (`ClassSoloWin`... counted once, by the class persistence when `PersistClassMatchResult` is on), Mix → `FreeWin/Lose`, Fes → `FesWin/Lose`; other online modes count in the totals only |
+| Player statistics | total given damage, enemies defeated, no-damage battles, EX burst damage, class 10-win streaks |
+| Per-suit statistics | `MobileSuitPvPStatistic`: battles, wins, damage, defeats per suit (the VS Mobile style tracker data) |
+| Burst-type statistics, daily challenge counters | as offline |
+| GP, player level / exp, navigator familiarity, suit mastery (use count), team skill points | `PersistOnlineProgress` (default `true`); the cabinet reports these deltas in `SaveVsmOnResult` like it does in the offline save, and each battle sends one save only (checked in the 2026-11-13..16 card-server logs: Mix / Class / Fes battles send `SaveVsmOnResult`, in-store worlds 15/16 send the offline `SaveVsmResult`, which was already stored in full), so nothing is applied twice; the captured online payloads carry the same per-battle deltas as offline ones (`level_exp` 10 after a loss in both) |
+
+Battle modes in the history: `online_matching_mode` + `shuffle_flag` → `ClassMatchSolo` / `ClassMatchTeam`
+(OMM_CLASS), `FreeSolo` / `FreeTeam` (OMM_FREE = Mix Match), `FesSolo` / `FesTeam` (OMM_FES), `OnlineOtherSolo` /
+`OnlineOtherTeam` (OMM_LOCAL, LOCATION, PRIVATE, PUB, EVENT).
+
+**Retries.** A result already stored for the same card (room id + `played_at` + suit + mode) is ignored completely
+(no second history row, no second win, GP or class-rate change): an in-memory key for 2 hours, and after a restart
+the stored history row (same card, `played_at`, mode, suit). A result with `played_at` = 0 is only de-duplicated in
+memory. Saves run one at a time (a retry that arrives while the first save still runs waits, then is recognised).
+**Failure.** The battle part runs in one DB transaction; if it fails (for example a damaged card without its stats
+row), it is rolled back and only the old badge + class part is stored; the cabinet still gets Success.
+**Switch off:** `"PersistOnlineBattleResults": false` → exactly the previous behaviour. No DB schema change (no
+migration); backing up `ServerInfinite.db` before swapping builds is still recommended.
+Only battles played with this build are recorded; earlier online games cannot be recovered. Partners / foes on
+other card servers show as "Player N" in the history (the result carries no names). Quick-start info in the online
+result is not saved (offline saves keep doing that).
+Tests: `Tests/Server.Tests` (15, in-memory SQLite with all migrations): Class solo, Class team, class W/L with the
+class persistence off, Mix solo / team, Fes, other modes, retry de-duplication (also after a restart), retry without
+timestamp, two battles in one room, two cards in one battle, flag off, progress off, unknown session, failure rollback.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
   (`BindMatchNodesToSourceIp` limits Check/Cancel to the IP that entered, but is not a login.)
